      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "We tested pretty heavily in Closed and Open Beta, as well as a few times in Live so far. One instance played several hour-long videos with zero desync, or pretty close. \n\nI'll add that if you are still getting it, one second of delay after 40 minutes is far, far better than the 5-10 seconds of delay we got in 5.6 after 5-10 minutes.\n\nThe bug was an issue on Unity's side, so if its continuing, that may be something that needs to be sought out with Unity. Can you reliably reproduce, and can you reliably reproduce in different worlds?",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
